From 7669e2c4828623c0c39ab6a124a31d9d4554b78f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: indextree <hellonypcteam@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:41:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] Add a sound Rust verifier, a layered-circuit builder
 and soundness tests

Upstream had no Rust verifier; its Python/circom verifiers trusted prover
supplied data. verifier::verify recomputes every challenge from the
transcript, enforces exact round counts and degree bounds, starts from
D~(z0) of the verifier's claimed output, checks each layer against the
verifier-side add~/mult~ wiring, and finally checks the verifier's own
input MLE. Prover hints (z, r, sumcheck_r, k, depth, d, input_func) are
ignored. Malformed proofs return errors instead of panicking.
